WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.803 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
♫♫

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:07.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, everybody.
Welcome back to "Corrections."

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:10.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let´s get started.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.114
the most problematic thing

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said during last week´s
"Corrections,"

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
based on the amount
of feedback I received.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:24.090
I said that I did something

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
"on" accident

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.595
instead of "by" accident.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.597 size:78% position:39%
People were outraged.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.766
This is a good sample comment

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
that someone wrote.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.903 size:81% position:41%
"You said that we are,

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:39.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
on accident,
doing jokes that are good.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:42.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
I cringe when I hear
someone say ´on´ accident

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.677
instead of ´by´ accident,

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
although in this case,
you probably should have said

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
´accidentally.´

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
To try to better myself,
I found my wife and asked her.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.520 size:84% position:42%
´Seth said on accident
instead of by accident.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.855
is that worthy of a correction?
Or should I leave him alone?´

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:58.858
She responded, ´Yes, it is.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.928 size:75% position:38%
That´s despicable.´"

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
So here we are.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:07.300 size:78% position:39%
So to that man, uh...

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
to his wife,

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
to everybody else
who was so upset,

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.339
I apologize, and I promise,

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.676
I did not do it by purpose.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said "invariably"
instead of "inevitably."

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.486 size:88% position:44%
I think I often do that.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.656 size:81% position:41%
And I am optimistic...

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:33.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
There will be
a future opportunity

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.162
for me to say it the right way,

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.498
because I believe that that...

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:41.668 size:78% position:39%
is certain to happen.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody said --
I talked about the fact

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:51.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I rented a Ford Festiva,
and a lot of people said,

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:54.481
"I can´t believe how many times
he said Festiva wrong."

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"It´s got to be Festiva."

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it Fest-iva?

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
It can´t be Fest-iva.
It´s Festiva.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I realized
a lot of people thought

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:03.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should be saying Fiesta,
a Ford Fiesta.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were both.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.759
There was a Ford Festiva.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.761
And then there is a Ford Fiesta,

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.263
and that seems like something

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:13.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
you should maybe
take up with Ford.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:18.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe Ford should be
a little bit less worried

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.540
about what Ferrari´s doing.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.513
The other thing about that is,

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was talking about
how when we rented,

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
when my brother and I
rented that Ford Festiva,

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:33.887
we would play Randy Newman,

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I Love L.A."

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did a few lines.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.625
A lot of people said
I have a terrible Randy Newman.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is incorrect.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s very good.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:48.401
[ As Newman ] Look at that bum,
down on his knees.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.903 size:84% position:42%
Look at those mountain,

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
look at old trees.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.545
[ Normal voice ] And I want
all of the jackals to know

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:02.448 size:81% position:41%
you do not [As Newman]
got the friend in me.

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:10.990
Renting the Ford Festiva is not
the worst car rental story

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.826 size:78% position:39%
I´ve ever had in L.A.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.062
Shoemaker and I were in L.A.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were staying in a hotel,
and we had --

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were there --

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.967 size:84% position:42%
I can´t even remember
what we were there for.

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe we were out there
for the Emmys or something.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had rented like,
let´s say, a Kia Optima.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
Something along the lines
of a Kia Optima.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.908
We were leaving our hotel,

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we gave the ticket
to the valet,

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:34.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were going
to get the Kia Optima.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:37.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Jason Statham
walked out

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
and gave the ticket
to the valet.

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:42.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just remember
my heart dropping.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.657 size:84% position:42%
´Cause all I hoped was,

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:48.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Please don´t have my car
come before Jason Statham´s,

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:51.764
who I´m sure has the coolest car

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
known to man."

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.036
And his car did show up first,

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember?
-Yeah.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was...

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
A Kia Optima.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:04.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.778 size:81% position:41%
I mean, souped up, no.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:09.782 size:78% position:39%
It was the lowest car
that I´ve ever seen,

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.452
and he got into -- he like --

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.020
It was like when you have --

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:17.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like a lie-flat seat
on an airplane.

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:20.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like he needed a periscope
to drive it.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was with --

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.796
I think he was
with Rosie Huntington-Whiteley.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.365 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah, I think he was.

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I mean,
if you already feel bad,

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
imagine if the guy
standing next to you

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
is with
Rosie Huntington-Whiteley

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:31.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you´re with...

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:33.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mikey "The Shoe."

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:39.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who´s already problematic
in L.A.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:43.616
I mean, if you think he´s
in a bad mood in New York City,

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.118
you should see this guy in L.A.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.619
And people know, you know --

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
They know
he´s a big-shot producer,

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he´s so --

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:50.690
You know, kids come up to him,

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.125
and they´re like, "Hey, Mikey,

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m a young actor.
You have a tip for me."

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.763
And he´s like, "Learn a trade."

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:59.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:07.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
Never -- I was --
And that was back --

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:10.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
When those "Fast Five" movies
started,

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was still --

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.246 size:78% position:39%
I was still an actor.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
Never asked...

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.750
to be in any of those films.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t -- I think if I was
in one of those movies,

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´d be one of those guys,
like, carrying --

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.424
on one side of a plate of glass,

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:28.094
you know, in the street,
like, "Whoa, steady, John."

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:31.097
And then it, like, cuts to...

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.266
Or I´d be like a guy with --

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:35.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, trying to hail a cab
with a coffee,

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, like,
a car would go...

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.805
and my coffee would be gone.

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:41.474
And they would just, like,
cut to Vin Diesel being like,

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:43.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
"[Bleep] latte."

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:48.915 size:75% position:38%
And I said I implied

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:50.249
that the last Blockbuster

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:53.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
closed in 2019.

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:57.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is one Blockbuster
left in Bend, Oregon.

00:05:57.757 --> 00:06:00.093
Bend, O-- And I guess there´s
been a Netflix documentary

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the last...

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:04.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
the last living Blockbuster
in Bend, Oregon.

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:07.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, crazy how
many corrections

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
we´re getting
from the state of Oregon

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.837 size:88% position:44%
that are cinema related.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:13.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, because we´ve talked
a lot about Astoria

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:16.609 size:78% position:39%
and how there is also
an Astoria in Oregon

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
how they have a film museum.

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:21.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now we know that the last
Blockbuster is in Oregon.

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.249
And the one thing, though,

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:25.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
is every time I mention
Astoria, Oregon,

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:28.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
I keep forgetting to say this,
is people there say,

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don´t know how you call it
in New York,

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:33.626
but we call it Ass-toria."

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:37.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I´m reluctant
to buy into that...

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:40.099
´cause it feels like a prank,

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:43.936
especially because they write
the "ass" part in all caps.

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:47.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also, they say
it´s pronounced "organ."

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:52.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bend, Organ.

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:56.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you know how you get
to Bend, Organ, Shoemaker?

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:00.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
You run into a brick wall
with the boner.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:03.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:11.831
Someone said, "Hey, this is from
last night´s ´Closer Look.´

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:14.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a note
for the correction --

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:18.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sorry, I have a note
for the graphics department.

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:21.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got a graphic
of a -- of a tornado

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.609 size:88% position:44%
on a New Jersey highway,

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:31.284
but graphics forgot to put
any bicycles on the highway,

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:33.152
and there -- there must --

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:35.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
there must be bicycles
on that highway

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.489 size:81% position:41%
because Seth called it

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:39.459
the New Jersey Turn-bike."

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:43.996
Now I don´t want to spend
a lot of time correcting --

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:45.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ll correct facts.

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:48.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
But flubs are just
a thing that happens.

00:07:48.835 --> 00:07:50.837 size:78% position:39%
That´s just the thing
that happens in life.

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:52.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
We´re not going to correct
all the flubs.

00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:56.676
Plus, I found it unlikely that
I said New Jersey Turn-bike.

00:07:56.676 --> 00:07:58.845
So I went back and took a look.

00:07:58.845 --> 00:07:59.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let´s see.

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:01.047
But it could´ve been a lot worse

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:04.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
if they hadn´t been stuck
in turn-bike traffic.

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let´s hear it again,
a little slower.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:07.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
Turn-bike traffic,

00:08:07.854 --> 00:08:10.022 size:84% position:42%
Okay. I said turn-bike.

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:14.327
So I´m not gonna blame the
graphics department for that,

00:08:14.327 --> 00:08:18.030 size:84% position:42%
but we did get a little
more flak on a graphic.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
We talked about...

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:20.967
how the flooding in New York

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:23.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
has led to a lot
of steps being taken,

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:26.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
up to and including
pigeons wearing snorkels.

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:28.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can we show
what graphics came up

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the pigeon
wearing a snorkel.

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:32.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now if you´re watching this
right now,

00:08:32.812 --> 00:08:35.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
can you guys jump
to the issue here?

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:36.449 size:84% position:42%
Okay, the issue here is

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:40.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
the snorkel doesn´t
cover the nostrils.

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:42.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
The mask...

00:08:42.388 --> 00:08:45.157
If the mask doesn´t cover

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:48.995
the nostrils, Graphics...

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:52.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
The pigeon dies,

00:08:52.098 --> 00:08:54.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:57.103 size:88% position:44%
and that´s not the joke.

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:00.273
I was so bummed last week

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:02.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I mentioned
Fine Young Cannibals,

00:09:02.275 --> 00:09:03.476 size:84% position:42%
and it was on Thursday,

00:09:03.476 --> 00:09:07.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Andy Samberg was here
because we did

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
a "Brooklyn Nine-Nine"
reunion show,

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:11.484 size:75% position:38%
and I didn´t realize
he was still here,

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:13.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought he´d left
to catch a flight,

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:14.687
and I wish I´d known he was here

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:17.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
because Andy does
an impression of Roland Gift,

00:09:17.857 --> 00:09:21.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
the lead singer of
Fine Young Cannibals,

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:22.528
and I would´ve had him come out,

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:23.896
So I don´t -- but I didn´t.

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:24.897 size:84% position:42%
So then I just thought,

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:27.066
Well, I´ll just FaceTime him now
and see.

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:29.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cellphone rings ]

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:31.637
Give me a second.
He does not know I´m doing this.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:39.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, I´m filming
"Corrections" right now.

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:41.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will you just do --

00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:43.082
sing "She Drives You Crazy"

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:46.419 size:78% position:39%
like Roland Gift from
Fine Young Cannibals.

00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:49.355 size:88% position:44%
-♫ She drives me crazy ♫

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:51.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
♫ Ooh, ooh-ooh ♫

00:09:51.357 --> 00:09:53.826 size:75% position:38%
♫ Like no one else ♫

00:09:53.826 --> 00:09:55.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
♫ Ooh, ooh-ooh ♫

00:09:55.528 --> 00:09:58.197 size:84% position:42%
♫ She drives me crazy ♫

00:09:58.197 --> 00:10:01.367
♫ And I can´t help myself ♫

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:03.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great. Thank you.
I love you, buddy.

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:04.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
So...

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:10:09.208 --> 00:10:11.043
I feel like we cleaned that up.

00:10:17.516 --> 00:10:19.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
We talked about how
a horse would smoke

00:10:19.018 --> 00:10:20.519
and it would hold a cigarette,

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was a lot
of talk about...

00:10:22.355 --> 00:10:23.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
it couldn´t hold it
with one hand,

00:10:23.689 --> 00:10:24.890
so it´d hold it like this.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:25.891
A lot of people said, actually,

00:10:25.891 --> 00:10:27.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
their hooves are
like fingernails,

00:10:27.994 --> 00:10:29.161 size:88% position:44%
which I don´t quite know

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:30.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
how that was supposed
to be helpful.

00:10:30.663 --> 00:10:32.231 size:75% position:38%
People said, really,
the issue is, like,

00:10:32.231 --> 00:10:34.266 size:88% position:44%
just it´s a joint issue.

00:10:34.266 --> 00:10:36.102
Their arms don´t bend like that.

00:10:36.102 --> 00:10:37.837
So, it wouldn´t matter how
they´d hold a cigarette.

00:10:37.837 --> 00:10:39.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
They could never
get it to their mouths.

00:10:39.505 --> 00:10:41.807
And then someone said, you know,

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:44.977 size:88% position:44%
at the end of the day...

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:47.213 size:78% position:39%
any animal who smokes

00:10:47.213 --> 00:10:49.281
is gonna end up a little hoarse.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.952
You know, I´m pretty disparaging

00:10:52.952 --> 00:10:56.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
about a lot of the things
you jackals say...

00:10:56.288 --> 00:10:58.624
But that´s the worst one.

00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:05.931 size:81% position:41%
We were missing an "L"

00:11:05.931 --> 00:11:08.534
in Cauliflower Doritos graphic.

00:11:08.534 --> 00:11:10.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can we take a look
at that again.

00:11:10.369 --> 00:11:13.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
As you notice, it´s not
how you spell Cauliflower.

00:11:13.372 --> 00:11:14.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
And --

00:11:14.974 --> 00:11:17.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we also talked about
how I have a bad Tom Brokaw.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those both came up
in corrections,

00:11:19.779 --> 00:11:22.481
and a couple of people...

00:11:22.481 --> 00:11:24.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
pointed this out,
and I got to say,

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:27.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is some real good work
by the jackals,

00:11:27.119 --> 00:11:29.455 size:78% position:39%
and you know how much
I hate to say that.

00:11:29.455 --> 00:11:31.023 size:75% position:38%
They said you really
miss an opportunity

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:33.359
because I feel like cauliflower
with only one "L"

00:11:33.359 --> 00:11:35.761
is how Tom Brokaw would say it.

00:11:35.761 --> 00:11:37.263
[ As Brokaw ] "Cauiflower."

00:11:37.263 --> 00:11:38.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:11:38.431 --> 00:11:40.766
[ Normal voice ] Not wrong.

00:11:40.766 --> 00:11:43.936 size:81% position:41%
[ As Brokaw ] Big news
in the chip community.

00:11:45.604 --> 00:11:47.940 size:75% position:38%
[ Speaks gibberish ]

00:11:50.576 --> 00:11:52.211 size:81% position:41%
We talked about Wally.

00:11:52.211 --> 00:11:55.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
That cue cards are
a part of Wally.

00:11:55.047 --> 00:11:57.383 size:75% position:38%
And that he was born
with the cue card,

00:11:57.383 --> 00:12:01.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I held up the cue card
he was born with.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.222 size:81% position:41%
That said, it´s a boy.

00:12:03.222 --> 00:12:07.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
And someone said,
so you amputated his cue card.

00:12:07.893 --> 00:12:11.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I did not,
and here´s the thing.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:14.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
Part of -- When a cue card
professional was born,

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:16.936 size:88% position:44%
part of the tradition --

00:12:16.936 --> 00:12:18.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is something
that I don´t think

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wally will be upset
that I´m saying --

00:12:20.339 --> 00:12:22.041
eight days after it´s born,

00:12:22.041 --> 00:12:25.544 size:81% position:41%
there is a ceremony...

00:12:25.544 --> 00:12:28.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:12:28.481 --> 00:12:32.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
...wherein a mohel
comes to the home

00:12:32.351 --> 00:12:34.520
and just snips off the cue card.

00:12:39.125 --> 00:12:40.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um...

00:12:40.292 --> 00:12:41.627 size:75% position:38%
Oh, I have really --

00:12:41.627 --> 00:12:46.465 size:84% position:42%
I have something really
exciting...to announce.

00:12:46.465 --> 00:12:48.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
A little emotional.

00:12:49.869 --> 00:12:51.370 size:75% position:38%
I got a new sweater.

00:12:56.408 --> 00:12:59.745
And this sweater was a gift

00:12:59.745 --> 00:13:02.314
that was sent here last week

00:13:02.314 --> 00:13:04.650
from my one time nemesis,

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:05.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
Patty Lyons.

00:13:05.718 --> 00:13:08.053
Patty is one of the members,

00:13:08.053 --> 00:13:09.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
a vocal member,
of the knitting community

00:13:09.755 --> 00:13:13.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
who has taken
a great amount of issue

00:13:13.492 --> 00:13:18.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
with errors I have made
over the past three months

00:13:18.164 --> 00:13:19.832
when I talked about knitting,

00:13:19.832 --> 00:13:22.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I have been
apologetic enough

00:13:22.601 --> 00:13:24.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Patty,

00:13:24.003 --> 00:13:27.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
in an effort
to bury the hatchet,

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.676
sewed me this beautiful sweater.

00:13:32.678 --> 00:13:34.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:13:38.551 --> 00:13:40.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my favorite thing
about it --

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:41.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there´s a lot
to like about it --

00:13:41.854 --> 00:13:44.356
You can wear it anywhere.

00:13:44.356 --> 00:13:47.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:13:48.227 --> 00:13:52.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
Formal. Casual.
it just goes great --

00:13:52.031 --> 00:13:53.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s just great.

00:13:55.568 --> 00:13:58.170 size:84% position:42%
That -- That´s an Emmy,

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:02.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
and "Corrections" did not
take home the Emmy,

00:14:02.908 --> 00:14:04.243 size:84% position:42%
finish tied for second.

00:14:04.243 --> 00:14:07.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not too shabby
for our first time out.

00:14:07.913 --> 00:14:09.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I will say

00:14:09.849 --> 00:14:12.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Emmys...

00:14:12.685 --> 00:14:14.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
are a dime a dozen.

00:14:14.186 --> 00:14:16.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to get an Emmy

00:14:16.589 --> 00:14:18.691 size:78% position:39%
on a homemade sweater

00:14:18.691 --> 00:14:19.992
from your one time nemesis,

00:14:19.992 --> 00:14:23.829
Patty Lyons, is a great deal

00:14:23.829 --> 00:14:26.832 size:75% position:38%
more valuable to me,

00:14:26.832 --> 00:14:29.168
and so I would just like to say

00:14:29.168 --> 00:14:31.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
to Patty...

00:14:31.837 --> 00:14:34.740
did you think for one second

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:38.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn´t know how
this was going to end?

00:14:38.244 --> 00:14:41.580
I walked into Shoemaker´s office
three months ago and said,

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I´m...

00:14:43.249 --> 00:14:45.584
going to get a new sweater.

00:14:45.584 --> 00:14:47.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:50.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said sweaters
can be expensive,

00:14:50.189 --> 00:14:52.791
and I said, Oh, I think I´ll...

00:14:52.791 --> 00:14:55.461
be getting my sweater for free.

00:14:55.461 --> 00:14:57.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:14:57.096 --> 00:14:58.497
Because there are three things

00:14:58.497 --> 00:15:01.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are true about
the knitting community.

00:15:01.667 --> 00:15:03.836 size:81% position:41%
They are foul mouthed.

00:15:03.836 --> 00:15:06.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
They are sensitive.

00:15:06.372 --> 00:15:08.941
And they are predictable.

00:15:08.941 --> 00:15:12.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I´m pretty sure
if I poke them...

00:15:12.444 --> 00:15:16.115
someone will inevitably...

00:15:16.115 --> 00:15:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:15:19.285 --> 00:15:22.288
...knit me a homemade sweater

00:15:22.288 --> 00:15:25.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
and send it my way.

00:15:25.124 --> 00:15:28.060
And Shoemaker said, you can do
all of that in three months?

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:29.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, buddy,

00:15:29.828 --> 00:15:33.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ve been working
on this for a decade,

00:15:33.332 --> 00:15:36.435 size:81% position:41%
when I took this photo

00:15:36.435 --> 00:15:38.437
of me knitting what is clearly

00:15:38.437 --> 00:15:41.941 size:75% position:38%
a crocheted blanket.

00:15:41.941 --> 00:15:44.276 size:78% position:39%
That was the first...

00:15:44.276 --> 00:15:46.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
piece of the trap.

00:15:46.111 --> 00:15:47.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:15:50.215 --> 00:15:51.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, Patty,

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:52.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess what
I´m trying to say is,

00:15:52.985 --> 00:15:56.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
sometimes in life,
you´re the knitter,

00:15:56.555 --> 00:15:59.892
and sometimes you´re the yarn.

00:16:05.464 --> 00:16:06.799
This has been "Corrections."

00:16:06.799 --> 00:16:09.802
Come back next week, won´t you?

00:16:09.802 --> 00:16:12.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:16:12.471 --> 00:16:14.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ll be here.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:20.179 size:75% position:38%
There´s a moth eggs.
She put [bleep] --

00:16:20.179 --> 00:16:22.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
There´s [bleep] moth eggs!
Patty!

